format_pe: no empty argument from empty cflags

fwupd-efi 1.8 runs uswid with an empty --cflags, and "".split(" ") is
[""]: the compiler is handed an empty argument and refuses it, so the
SBOM section is never made and the build stops. split() with no
separator gives no arguments from an empty string.

Signed-off-by: Jax Carls <jax.carls@protonmail.com>
--- a/uswid/format_pe.py
+++ b/uswid/format_pe.py
@@ -83,7 +83,7 @@
         if not cc:
             raise NotSupportedError("compiler is required for missing section")
         subprocess.run(
-            [cc, "-x", "c", "-c", "-o", filepath, "/dev/null"] + cflags.split(" "),
+            [cc, "-x", "c", "-c", "-o", filepath, "/dev/null"] + cflags.split(),
             check=True,
         )
 
